 "result_text": "`DefFrame` now supports `CHANNEL-DELAY`.\n\n- **Constructing:** there is a new optional `channel_delay` field, added last so existing positional arguments still work.\n- **Parsing:** `CHANNEL-DELAY` is accepted as a frame attribute in the grammar and mapped to `channel_delay` in the parser.\n- **Stringifying:** `DefFrame.out()` writes `CHANNEL-DELAY` after the other options.\n\nI also added `CHANNEL-DELAY` to the reserved keyword list in `pyquil/quilbase.py`, next to `INITIAL-FREQUENCY`.\n\nI checked it by parsing a program with `CHANNEL-DELAY: 1e-07` in a `DEFFRAME`. The parsed `DefFrame` had `channel_delay=1e-07`, and the output text included it. I didn't run the test suite.\n\nThe changes are in `pyquil/quilbase.py`, `pyquil/_parser/grammar.lark` and `pyquil/_parser/parser.py`. I haven't committed anything.",
